  "id": "COMPOUND:4783 - PROTEIN:4299",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Pleconaril may interact with Sodium/Potassium Transporting ATPase subunits through a series of molecular targets. Specifically, Pleconaril is shown to target G1/S-specific cyclin-D1, which is a target of both (1S,5S,6S,13R,21S)-5,13-bis(4-hydroxyphenyl)-4,12,14-trioxapentacyclo[11.7.1.02,11.03,8.015,20]henicosa-2(11),3(8),9,15,17,19-hexaene-6,9,17,19,21-pentol and Senegose A. Both of these compounds are identified as targets of the Sodium/Potassium Transporting ATPase subunits. This indicates that Pleconaril may exert its effects by modulating the activity of these ATPase subunits, potentially through the regulation of cyclin-D1 expression. The evidence suggests a possible mechanism involving the modulation of cyclin-D1, which in turn may influence the activity of the Sodium/Potassium Transporting ATPase subunits. The strength of the evidence is consistent across multiple paths, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
